lt is a reproducible signing and entitlement baseline for later M0 integration, not a production VPN.","id":"STORY-260715-2xnj3v","isBlocked":false,"name":"apple-capability-provisioning","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: organization enrollment and required roles; bundle ID, App Group, and Keychain access-group naming; Network Extension packet-tunnel capabilities; development certificates and profiles; disposable iOS and macOS host/provider probes; NETunnelProviderManager configuration; entitlement and embedded-profile inspection; physical-device install, launch, start, and stop evidence. Out of scope: TestFlight or App Store release, Developer ID notarization, production UI, packet forwarding, SSH transport, relay behavior, and storage of certificates, private keys, credentials, or provisioning secrets in the repository or board.","status":"to-dev","title":"Gate P0 — Apple capabilities and physical-device provisioning","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. The spike uses only NEPacketTunnelFlow and documented Darwin socket APIs and contains no utun control access, descriptor discovery, or private API. 2. Forward and reverse paths preserve packet boundaries, add or validate and strip network-byte-order AF_INET or AF_INET6 headers, batch writes, and count malformed or unsupported frames. 3. EAGAIN, EWOULDBLOCK, and ENOBUFS cause bounded reason-specific drops; EMSGSIZE fails start with attempted and effective limits; persistent errors and cancellation release all tasks and descriptors. 4. Upstream HEV runs with socks5.udp set to tcp and the stated low-memory baseline, and its internal SOCKS endpoint rejects unowned ingress. 5. Swift Testing and fault-injection coverage verifies framing, batching budgets, saturation, MTU errors, cleanup, repeated start and stop, IPv4, and IPv6. 6. Physical iPhone and macOS evidence covers MTUs 1500, 4096, and 8500; constrained buffers; recei