ne scheduling, full application UX, and performance claims not backed by before-and-after measurements.","status":"to-dev","title":"M0 packetFlow, socket-pair, and HEV bridge spike","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. An architecture decision records the chosen generator, exact supported deployment targets, target graph, module ownership, dependency direction, configuration strategy, and reasons against viable alternatives. 2. Clean generation produces buildable ReluxProxyMac, ReluxProxyMacTunnel, ReluxProxyIOS, ReluxProxyIOSTunnel, ReluxTunnelCore, ReluxTunnelHarness, relux-relay, and protocol-test targets with deterministic identifiers and schemes. 3. Both providers are thin adapters that depend on shared core contracts and do not duplicate packet, SSH, relay, lifecycle, or memory state machines. 4. Native Swift and C dependencies can be pinned, licensed, and linked without dynamic-library or App Store extension violations. 5. Credential-free CI or local verification builds every target and runs shared tests; signed physical-device configurations consume Gate P0 identities without committing secrets. 6. The existing SwiftPM tests, manual SOCKS app build, defaults, and release path remain reproducible until an explicit migration decision says otherwise. 7. Developer documentation explains generation, target ownership, signing inputs, artifact locations, and how to run the harness.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["STORY-260715-2itwz7","STORY-260715-2xnj3v"],"blocks":["STORY-260715-jnpbyz","STORY-260715-lkshfz"],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-14lk3y","TASK-260715-1ccx3l","TASK-260715-1fv4z1","TASK-260715-1g9cyt","TASK-260715-2btjwm","TASK-260715-2nfz7w","TASK-260715-32umrc","TASK-260715-33oofa","TASK-260715-3bdplx","TASK-260715-3r0993","TASK-260715-d6x51z","TASK-260715-nphtib","TASK-260715-pmww4f","TASK-260715-sbrrp7","TASK-260715-uyju7n"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Replace the single-target SwiftPM-only project shape with a reproducibly generated Apple workspace foundation that can embed iOS and macOS packet-tunnel extensions while preserving the currently shipped macOS SOCKS application until a separate migration decision retires or replaces it. Establish thin platform adapters, a shared ReluxTunnelCore boundary, native dependency seams, a fast macOS harness, and relay target placeholders without implementing production tunnel behavior.","id":"STORY-260715-l2i2oo","isBlocked":true,"name":"target-project-architecture","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: current-state and migration inventory; Tuist-versus-alternative and deployment-target evidence; target and configuration graph; iOS and macOS host and packet-tunnel targets; ReluxTunnelCore Swift package; ReluxTunnelHarness CLI; portable relux-relay and protocol-test target shells; signing configuration seams; pinned native dependency integration strategy; clean generation, build, and test verification; legacy SwiftPM and release-path preservation; developer documentation. Out of scope: production packet forwarding, SSH engine selection, UDP relay protocol implementation, profile UX migration, full release automation, App Store submission, and retirement of the existing system-SSH app.","status":"to-dev","title":"Generated Apple multi-target project foundation","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"},{"ac":"1. Both candidates build in the macOS and iOS packet-tunnel target configurations, with pinned revisions, licenses, integration constraints, and reproducible build commands recorded. 2. One common conformance harness obtains raw host-key evidence before acceptance and exercises Ed25519 plus an approved fallback against current OpenSSH, documented older profiles, and the real relux host. 3. Candidate evidence covers independent direct-tcpip and bidirectional long-lived exec channels, early close and half-close, bounded backpressure, cancellation, network loss, reconnect, and no task, channel, socket, or descriptor growth across repeated cycles. 4. Initial receive windows and WINDOW_ADJUST behavior are configurable per channel; tests cover 32 KiB, 64 KiB, and capped bandwidth-delay-product profiles without multiplying a large default by maximum sessions. 5. Client byte and time thresholds and server requests survive at least 5 GiB of simultaneous direct-tcpip and exec traffic, with lane-local failure evidence. 6. Hundreds of concurrent channels and one, two, and four connection trials remain within the extension memory budget and record device, OS, revisions, algorithms, traffic, loss and latency, windows, queued bytes, CPU, physical footprint, peak, and failures. 7. A decision record selects only a candidate that passes every required gate, documents rejected results and residual risks, and routes a red primary candidate to the alternate rather than weakening criteria.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["STORY-260715-l2i2oo","STORY-260715-2xnj3v","STORY-260715-jnpbyz"],"blocks":[],"checklist":[],"children":["TASK-260715-1af33i","TASK-260715-1gjxer","TASK-260715-1ozsb6","TASK-260715-1u2vpc","TASK-260715-28ok1k","TASK-260715-2d3g5e","TASK-260715-2ny6z4","TASK-260715-2xx2tk","TASK-260715-39xz9g","TASK-260715-3ikonq","TASK-260715-nzdzv3"],"created":"2026-07-15T00:46:59Z","description":"Compare a minimal, upstream-trackable ReluxNIOSSH fork with libssh2 behind one spike transport contract and select an in-process engine only after one candidate passes the complete Apple-target, host-verification, authentication, direct-tcpip, exec, window, rekey, compatibility, backpressure, cancellation, lifecycle, and memory matrix.","id":"STORY-260715-lkshfz","isBlocked":true,"name":"ssh-engine-spike","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"EPIC-260715-2mqgvm","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: pinned candidate revisions and licenses; iOS and macOS packet-tunnel-compatible static or source integration; raw host-key evidence; Ed25519 and approved fallback authentication; direct-tcpip and bidirectional exec channels; bounded writes; per-channel initial windows and adjustment policy; client byte and time rekey plus server rekey; keepalive, cancellation, metrics, and error mapping; current and supported older OpenSSH profiles plus the real relux server; hundreds of channels; at least 5 GiB mixed traffic; one, two, and four raw SSH connections; loss, reconnect, and descriptor tests; memory comparison; engine ADR and fork maintenance plan. Out of scope: SFTP, interactive shells, agent or X11 forwarding, password prompts, ProxyJump, production lane scheduling or flow migration, QUIC policy implementation, remote relay implementation, and weakening a failed gate to preserve a preferred candidate.","status":"to-dev","title":"M0 in-process SSH engine comparison and selection","type":"story","updated":"2026-07-15T01:09:28Z"}]

